      "claim": "The dominant economic relationship between medieval English lords and peasants was feudal, based on obligatory labor services, rents, and dues rather than voluntary market exchange.",
      "evidence": "Manorial court rolls, Domesday Book entries, and modern scholarship (e.g., Bloch, 1961; Hilton, 1975) describe peasants owing corvée labor, a portion of their harvest, and various fees to their lord.",
      "weight": 0.35,
      "depends_on": []
